<!--
  ats_invalid_zero_establishment.xml — the establishment branch code is "000".

  Which element carries the rule is the whole point of this fixture, and the
  answer is not the obvious one.

  THE RULE IS NOT ON detalleCompras/establecimiento. "000" is rejected here
  because it sits on iva/numEstabRuc, whose type numEstabRucType
  (ats.xsd:1482-1489) is based on xsd:integer with minExclusive 000 at
  ats.xsd:1484, maxInclusive 999 at ats.xsd:1485 and pattern \d{3} at
  ats.xsd:1487. "000" collapses to the integer 0, which is not greater than 0.

  THE NEAR-MISS: detalleCompras/establecimiento (ats.xsd:734-735) is typed
  establecimientoType (ats.xsd:26-30), which is based on xsd:string and carries
  only the pattern [0-9]{3} — no minInclusive, no minExclusive. "000" therefore
  VALIDATES there. The companion fixture assertion in
  test_zero_establishment_is_rejected_where_the_rule_exists documents that
  acceptance so the gap is recorded rather than assumed away.

  minExclusive 000 exists in exactly two places in the whole schema:
  numEstabRucType (ats.xsd:1484) and ventasEstabType (ats.xsd:1470), the latter
  typed onto ventasEstablecimiento/ventaEst/codEstab (ats.xsd:1463). Both are
  xsd:integer. Any element of type establecimientoType is unguarded.

  Element under test: iva/numEstabRuc, ats.xsd:602-604 (minOccurs="0").
-->
